;; expect: main.one link-error link_cycle
;; roots: main.shard a b
;; link: yes
;; two implementations each proved from the other's law: each check passes in its own fork,
;; where the other's function and law are parameters, and both discharges are recorded. There
;; is no environment in which both names are their implementations — `fa` would be defined
;; by `fb` and `fb` by `fa` — and the link finds none: the consumer's theorem stays what it
;; was, a fact about any `fa` with the law
(import "a")
(import "b")
(use a)
(theorem one () (= fa 1) (exact fa_is))
